# Recipes .github/workflows/ci.yml runs that `just test-all` deliberately does
# NOT reach. Enforced by scripts/check-ci-parity.sh (in `just check`).
#
# Format: one recipe name per line. An entry is a RECORDED DECISION — say why,
# or it is just an oversight with better paperwork. Entries whose CI step is
# gone fail the gate, so this file cannot rot.

# SMP=2 real-parallelism lane (MTTCG). Inherently non-deterministic — host
# scheduling variance makes its timing proofs flaky — so it retries (bounded) in
# CI and is kept out of the pre-commit loop. test-all runs the DETERMINISTIC
# 1-hart equivalent instead (`ci-os-smp1`, -smp 1 + icount), which covers the
# same marker ladder without the flake.
ci-os-smp

# Provisioning, not a gate: `inputs` is a dependency edge of every recipe that
# compiles the workspace, so test-all pulls it in implicitly on its first
# compiling step. CI's qemu job calls it explicitly only because that job shells
# out to scripts/qemu-test.sh directly instead of going through a recipe.
inputs

# NOTE — not expressible here: the qemu job's first lane runs
# `./scripts/qemu-test.sh --profile=headless` directly rather than via a recipe,
# so the parity gate cannot see it. test-all covers the same ladder through
# `ci-os-smp1` (profile smp1). If that direct call ever becomes `just
# ci-os-headless`, the gate will start seeing it and this note can go.
